#? Managed by provisioning — roles/btop_config/templates/btop.conf.j2
#? Do not edit this file: re-provisioning overwrites it. btop has NO include
#? mechanism (there is no local.conf overlay), so this file is the whole
#? managed config.
#?
#? Exactly two settings are set. Every other btop setting is deliberately
#? ABSENT so btop applies its own stock defaults (design decision D6: no
#? graph_symbol / presets / update_ms / proc_sorting tuning — the diff stays
#? auditable and the surface small).
#?
#? color_theme — matched BY FILENAME against the themes btop discovered while
#? scanning $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/btop/themes at startup. An absolute path to a file
#? outside the scanned dirs resolves to nothing and falls back to the built-in
#? Default_theme SILENTLY (btop_theme.cpp:451-471), which is why this is a
#? filename and not a path to the runtime's current/. The file it names is a
#? runtime consumer pointer at
#? <install>/config/btop/themes/colors.btop.theme ->
#? <state>/dotfiles/current/colors.btop.theme.
#? Theme::updateThemes (:430-442) filters on extension() == ".theme" (lexical,
#? reads the LINK's own name) and access(R_OK) (follows the chain), so the
#? symlink is invisible to btop.
#?
#? NOTE the value is the FILE's basename (colors.btop.theme), NOT a
#? csg-prefixed alias. setTheme compares `color_theme` against the discovered
#? entries by full path, filename, or STEM — a value that matches none of those
#? is not an error, it is a silent fallback to Default_theme, which is exactly
#? the failure this integration exists to prevent.
#?
#? save_config_on_exit — MANDATORY, not cosmetic. btop defaults it to true
#? (btop_config.cpp:379) and Config::write() truncates and rewrites the whole
#? config on exit (:836-845). ~/.config/btop is a symlink into the git-tracked
#? install spine, so with the default every btop quit would overwrite the
#? provisioning-owned btop.conf THROUGH the symlink and land the user's UI
#? changes in version control. This line is what prevents that.
#?
#? Reload: btop honours SIGUSR2 as a full config + theme hot reload
#? (btop.cpp:1053 -> reload_conf -> init_config + Theme::updateThemes() +
#? Theme::setTheme()). The runtime's BtopReloader sends it on every
#? palette swap, so an OPEN btop re-themes live. Provisioning itself
#? never signals a running btop — that is the runtime's job, and it
#? happens only after the consumer pointer has been repointed.

color_theme = "colors.btop.theme"
save_config_on_exit = false